'''armigerous''' (är-mij′e-rus), ''a.'' [< L. ''armiger'' (later, but rarely, ''armigerus''), bearing arms: see ''armiger''.] Entitled to bear heraldic arms.
{{smaller block|They belonged to the ''armigerous'' part of the population.
